! la_guess_ibox_inflight.strap -- a wrong guess is not undone by an I-box
! instruction that was still waiting on its read when the branch resolved.
!
! WHY IT EXISTS.  The instruction unit guesses a branch on an arithmetic
! indicator not taken and runs on (docs/microarchitecture_plan.md stage
! 3c).  An I-box instruction on the fall-through path that reads storage
! (here LV, its index word) is held in the E-box until the read answers.
! The model let the branch level leave the look-ahead while that LV was
! held.  On a wrong guess rl_recover set the counter to the target, and on
! the next clock rl_exec_resume finished the LV and committed its own next
! address over the target, so the fall-through ran as if the guess had
! been right.
!
! FOUND 2026-11-14 by the 7030 STRAP II's TABMAN (decks/strap2_7030.strap,
! TBMOV's backward loop: "KI(BU,24),0; BZAE,TBMB1" then "LV,$3,TBMLK;
! B,0($3)"), which lost a loop step whenever the LV's read was slow enough,
! that is, at some code alignments and not others.  This deck repeats that
! loop shape: count down K from 3, close with KI 0 and BZAE, and leave by
! LV,$3 and B,0($3).  Whether the LV is still in flight when the branch
! resolves is timing, so the four loops differ only in 0-3 extra E-box
! loads at the top.
!
! EXPECTED, derived by hand: every loop runs three times, so CNT1-CNT4 are
! each 3 (in bits 0-15), and the program ends at DONE.
!
! MEASURED INJECTION (headReady's !ebox.busy() put back to the old
! !ebox.busyFor(OwnerLA)): exactly CNT3 fails, 1 instead of 3; CNT1, CNT2
! and CNT4 pass.  So only one of the four timings exposes the bug, which is
! why there are four.

        SLC, (8)200.0
START   NOP
LOOP1   M+1(BU,16), CNT1
        L(BU,24), K1
        -(BU,24), ONE
        ST(BU,24), K1
        KI(BU,24), 0
        BZAE, LOOP1
        LV, $3, RET1
        B, 0($3)
END1    NOP
LOOP2   M+1(BU,16), CNT2
        L(BU,24), ONE
        L(BU,24), K2
        -(BU,24), ONE
        ST(BU,24), K2
        KI(BU,24), 0
        BZAE, LOOP2
        LV, $3, RET2
        B, 0($3)
END2    NOP
LOOP3   M+1(BU,16), CNT3
        L(BU,24), ONE
        L(BU,24), ONE
        L(BU,24), K3
        -(BU,24), ONE
        ST(BU,24), K3
        KI(BU,24), 0
        BZAE, LOOP3
        LV, $3, RET3
        B, 0($3)
END3    NOP
LOOP4   M+1(BU,16), CNT4
        L(BU,24), ONE
        L(BU,24), ONE
        L(BU,24), ONE
        L(BU,24), K4
        -(BU,24), ONE
        ST(BU,24), K4
        KI(BU,24), 0
        BZAE, LOOP4
        LV, $3, RET4
        B, 0($3)
END4    NOP
DONE    BEW,$
        CNOP

        SLC, (8)400.0
ONE     DD(BU,64), (16)0000010000000000
K1      DD(BU,64), (16)0000030000000000
K2      DD(BU,64), (16)0000030000000000
K3      DD(BU,64), (16)0000030000000000
K4      DD(BU,64), (16)0000030000000000
RET1    XW, END1, 0, 0
RET2    XW, END2, 0, 0
RET3    XW, END3, 0, 0
RET4    XW, END4, 0, 0
        SLC, (8)420.0
CNT1    DD(BU,64), 0
CNT2    DD(BU,64), 0
CNT3    DD(BU,64), 0
CNT4    DD(BU,64), 0
        END, START
